        "comments": "The assembly cbAmpLapp4.1 is based on 74x PacBio data and Arima2 Hi-C data generated by the Darwin Tree of Life Project\n(https://www.darwintreeoflife.org/). The assembly process included the following sequence of steps: initial PacBio assembly generation with Hifiasm, and Hi-C based scaffolding with YaHS. The mitochondrial and chloroplast genomes were assembled using OATK. Finally, the primary assembly was analysed and manually improved using TreeVal. Chromosome-scale scaffolds confirmed by the Hi-C data have been named in order of size. The reported karyotype for this species is n=16. This assembly contains 15 chromosomes.However, the smallest of the chromosomes, Chromosome 15, has double the coverage of the other autosomes. This indicates that there should indeed be another very similar chromosome that has been collapsed by the assembler into one chromosome.",
